  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for how much light is reflected, book page 216, topic 8.2.1, চিত্র ৮.০৫. A boy, a red hibiscus at the height of his eye, and between them a slab of clear glass on a lab jack. The student lifts the glass (a tap or a drag) and the light meets it at a larger and larger angle of incidence, from 30° to 87°. The reflected ray grows and the refracted ray thins, each as thick as the light it carries, by Fresnel's equations for n = 1.5; a small picture shows what the boy really sees, the pattern under the glass fading as the flower comes up in it; a graph in the panel follows. Five test questions. Offline, Bangla and English.",
